  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trees Outside Forests in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  .USAID will invest FY 2022.funds in the Trees Outside Forests in India (TOFI) activity to expand the.planting of trees outside of forests in India for enhanced provision of.ecosystem services, especially carbon sequestration, and increased inclusive.economic opportunities. USAID will provide technical assistance to the.Government of India (GOI) and other stakeholders to: strengthen an enabling.environment that promotes and incentivizes farmers and other tree growers to.plant trees; increase economic opportunities from trees outside of forests through.interventions, such as increasing availability of high quality planting.material, demonstration of quality plantations, promoting wood-based value.chains and financing; and improve access to technical information necessary to.ensure the success and viability of tree-based production systems outside of.forests. The activity will contribute to reducing pressure on forest reserves.for timber, fuelwood and fodder. It will also address forest degradation and.help the GOI meet its target of creating an additional carbon sink of 2.5 to 3.billion tons of CO2 equivalent by 2030. This activity aligns with the U.S.Government&apos;s strategy to address climate change through nature-based solutions.and will support the forestry pillar of the U.S.-India Climate Action and.Finance Mobilization Dialogue... .</narrative>
  </description>
